    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d463">

                <pb facs="0841" n="827" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg827"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Field, Acting Attorney-General, to Mr. Davis, Acting
                        Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Attorney-General’s
                            Office</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>,
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1869-08-16"><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >August</hi> 16, 1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith
                    copies of a telegram, received Saturday evening last, from the United States
                    marshal at New York, and a telegram sent the same evening to the United States
                    district attorney at Philadelphia, relative to the steamer Hornet; also a
                    telegram just received from the assistant district attorney at Philadelphia,
                    relating to the same vessel.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, yours, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. A. FIELD,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting Attorney
                        General.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. C. B. Davis</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>




